
Implementation notes:

17DEC2024 @hanoihantrakul 
WARNING! WARNING! This implementation
uses torch_wav2spec() which hardcodes f_max=12000 under the hood.
Even if you are training at 44.1khz, the underlying mel transformation
only encodes up to 12khz causing all my results using this class to be incorrect!

25NOV2024 @hanoihantrakul
In order to load stereo data from the same dataset as Wei Tsung's vocoder training,
I switched the dataloader for stereo FrozenUMM-Mel-Decoder to using Wei Tsung's old
decoder class. His code is from JUN2024 and there was a funny bug regarding BytesIO 
in this implementation when using the latest samantha image (1.0.0.133). I couldn't 
figure out how to fix this, and so just left it because training could still proceed.

`samantha.dataio.parquet.extension - WARNING - expected str, bytes or os.PathLike object, not BytesIO` 

The data ID used is 2196, which is identical to Wei Tsung's reference vocoder training trial.

These configs reconstruct audio using the `torch_wav2spec()` function, which is not compatible
with GriffinLim inversion.